  'ea6aee1a-e625-5cdd-8cbe-3a23e044cc53', '5aa7c891-fff7-52e4-bfea-7d8810019077',
  'In this exercise, we will use **Standard Template Library List** to implement a Data Log. This is a simple implementation in applications using undo and redo. For example in Microsoft Word, you must have nodes to store states when Ctrl+Z or Ctrl+Shift+Z to go back or forward. DataLog has a doubly linked list to store the states of data (an integer) and iterator to mark the current state. Each state is stored in a node, the transition of states is depicted in the figure below.

picture/image.png

```cpp
class DataLog
{
private:
    list<int> logList;
    list<int>::iterator currentState;

public:
    DataLog();
    DataLog(const int &data);
    void addCurrentState(int number);
    void subtractCurrentState(int number);
    void save();
    void undo();
    void redo();

    int getCurrentStateData()
    {
        return *currentState;
    }

    void printLog()
    {
        for (auto i = logList.begin(); i != logList.end(); i++) {
            if(i == currentState) cout << "Current state: ";
            cout << "[" << *i << "] => ";
        }
        cout << "END_LOG";
    }
};
```

